Appendix F — IIT / \Phi Exploratory Annex

F.1 Status

The measurement of \Phi is not a pillar of falsification for the Continuity Gap framework. This annex exists to record what would and would not be informative if \Phi-proxies were used.

F.2 Reasons for Exclusion

1. IIT is a theory of protoconsciousness, not phenomenal consciousness.
2. \Phi is not well-defined for general physical systems.
3. Computational cost of \Phi grows faster than exponentially with system size.
4. Independent replication of \Phi values across implementations is unreliable.

F.3 What Would Count as Informative

If a future theory T provided:

· an operational definition of a quantity C_\Phi^T,
· an intersubjectively reproducible measurement protocol for C_\Phi^T,
· a falsifiable prediction linking C_\Phi^T to C_\Phi,

then C_\Phi^T could be admitted as a proxy for C_\Phi. No such theory is currently available.

F.4 Prohibition on Overclaiming

Any result reported in this framework must not use \Phi-proxies to support claims about Q₂. Proxy results may be reported in a clearly labeled exploratory section, but they do not enter the main falsification design.

